  "narrative": {
    "intro": "CACI Federal reported $2B in contract obligations for FY2026 to date. CACI Federal received 183 awards so far, with an average award size of $11.2M, and obligations were down 42.0% year over year. The Department of Defense accounted for $1B of obligations, making DoD the largest buyer by far, followed by the General Services Administration at $721M. Computer Systems Design Services led CACI Federal’s NAICS markets with $827M, and Engineering Services followed with $506M. Smaller markets included Investigation and Personal Background Check Services at $186M and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences at $155M. Fiscal-year comparisons show prior-year totals of $1.3B in FY21, $1.7B in FY22, $2.3B in FY23, $2.8B in FY24, and $3.5B in FY25. The current-year totals are partial and represent year-to-date obligations rather than full fiscal-year totals. The concentration in a few agencies and NAICS sectors is evident from the dollar values, and the year-over-year decline reflects lower obligations compared with the prior fiscal year totals.",
    "sections": [
