        "heading": "What explains the FY2026 to date totals?",
        "body": "CACI Federal recorded $2B in obligations through FY2026 to date, down 42.0% year over year. The Department of Defense accounted for $1B of those obligations and the General Services Administration accounted for $721M, concentrating most obligations in two buyers. Prior-year fiscal totals show a rise through FY25, which provides context for the current-year decline."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where are CACI Federal’s obligations concentrated?",
        "body": "CACI Federal’s obligations are concentrated in Computer Systems Design Services at $827M and Engineering Services at $506M. The Department of Defense is the top buyer with $1B, followed by the General Services Administration with $721M. Several smaller markets and agencies account for the remaining obligations."
      }
